# 20. GAME LOGIC INVARIANTS

Enforce the following invariants:

- Exactly one active moving block exists during MOVING state.
- Every successful placement increases score exactly once.
- A missed placement never increases score.
- Successful retained width never exceeds previous block width.
- Retained width is never negative.
- A perfect placement retains exactly the previous width.
- A partial placement retains exactly the positive overlap width.
- A new block always inherits the latest retained width.
- A placed block never changes position after final resolution.
- Only one placement resolution may execute at a time.
- Game over is triggered at most once per run.
- Restart creates a fresh run without stale animations or callbacks.
- Hiding or showing overlays never changes the stored block geometry.
- Pausing and resuming does not alter the current score or block position.
- Theme changes never alter collision behavior or gameplay difficulty.

These rules should be reflected in code and automated tests.

